Hmm...so just to be clear, you are having a problem getting the Psychotria example to run, when you copy the commands directly from the example script on PhyloWiki without modification, and without skipping anything from the start of the script?  I'll proceed on this basis...

It's almost like it crashes on the first matrix exponentiation calculation, so I'm wondering if you have rexpokit and cladoRcpp successfully installed?  Typically, this all installs automatically, but if you had a crash somewhere in the install process, it is conceivable it didn't tell you.

So,

1. Tell me your operating system

2. Try each of these, one-by-one, and report back what you get, if there are problems:

sessionInfo()
install.packages("rexpokit", dependencies=TRUE))
install.packages("cladoRcpp", dependencies=TRUE)
install.packages("BioGeoBEARS", dependencies=TRUE)

...if these all work, try running the example script again, from the top through just the DEC optimization, line by line looking for error messages (warnings are typically OK).

Cheers!
Nick

